<title>USA: Intermedia buys NetSolve for $12.3 mln.</title>
<headline>Intermedia buys NetSolve for $12.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intermedia Communications Inc said on Tuesday it acquired the assets of the data transport business of NetSolve Inc for $12.3 million in cash.</p>
<p>The sale closed December 30, 1996.</p>
<p>NetSolve's data transport business generates about $16 million of recurring annual revenues, the company said.</p>
<p>Intermedia said about 50 percent of the companies' routes overlap, allowing the company to combine traffic on the two networks for meaningful economies of scale.</p>
</text>
